! mcp_bootstrap_p160.strap -- the tail of the LOCATE PSEUDO-OP
! (K FINI), the illegal-request exit (K ILEGL), the status-
! evaluation locate entry (K K LOC), the post-locate bookkeeping
! (K POST L) and the select-the-unit subroutine (K G LOC),
! printed page 160.  docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.167, header
! READ and not assumed: the top line prints "TIME CLOCK 00054041
! PUNID 11D11MCP   CARD ID IE000047   DIST. OF 3/01   3/01
! PAGE NUMBER  160", and the column-heading row's own
! "LOCATION  220057" names line 1's word.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE PAGE IS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THIRTY-FOUR PRINTED LINES AND NOT ONE OF THEM IS QUIET.  Every
! line compiles bits.  There is no SLC, no banner, no comment
! card, no DD/SYN/VF and no reservation on this page: thirty-four
! instructions, twenty-two half words and twelve full words, and
! then blank paper to the foot of the form.
!
! Five entry points, back to back:
!
!   lines  1-7   K FINI, the tail of the LOCATE pseudo-op.  It
!                sets the condition code to 16, moves S ARC AD
!                into S CU ARC (the requested arc becomes the
!                current arc), and tests the SELECT bit
!                S SEL($11).  If the unit is not already in
!                select it goes round K ILEGL's first card into
!                K ILEGL.32; otherwise it calls the select
!                subroutine (SIC,K G LOCR ; B,K G LOC) and then
!                leaves the same way.
!
!   lines  8-10  K ILEGL, the illegal-request exit: load condition
!                code 0o400 (fake an EPGK), set the return to
!                K NORM and go to K GATE.  Its SECOND half word,
!                K ILEGL.32, is the normal exit, which is why
!                lines 4 and 7 both branch to K ILEGL.32 and not
!                to K ILEGL.
!
!   lines 11-14  K K LOC, the status-evaluation entry to the
!                locate subroutine.  C22-6728 (MCP System Analysis
!                Guide) printed p.172 describes these four cards
!                in English: "the appropriate entry in the branch
!                table should be B, KKLOC, where the routine at
!                KKLOC sets the KLOCAT return to ZSTEVL, and sets
!                SRETAD in the event the equipment is disk".  Line
!                11 is LVI,9,Z STEVL and line 12 SVA,9,K LOCTD --
!                that is "sets the KLOCAT return to ZSTEVL".  Line
!                13's SIC and line 14's branch are "sets SRETAD",
!                and the saved IC is 220067.40, which is
!                K K LOC + 2.0 exactly; Figure 94's own box reads
!                "SET KLOCAT RETURN TO ZSTVL, SET SRETAD TO
!                KKLOC+2.0" and the guide's index carries the
!                entry "KKLOC+2.0".  See WITNESSES below.
!
!   lines 15-22  K K LOC + 2.0, where the locate interrupt comes
!                back.  Tests index 4, clears the locate-suppress
!                bit S LOC SU, calls the I/O-indicator check
!                (SIC,E IND R ; B,E IO IND -- the calling sequence
!                printed in full on printed p.189), then calls
!                K POST L and leaves to Z STEVL.
!
!   lines 23-27  K POST L: take the arc address out of the last
!                I/O instruction (S IO INS+.32), store it as both
!                S ARC AD and S CU ARC, drop the SELECT bit, and
!                return through K POSLD's B,$.
!
!   lines 28-34  K G LOC, "-TURN ON SEL BIT FOR LAST UNIT".  It
!                loads the unit-area value, adds the unit number
!                shifted left 18, indexes $9 by it (V+,9,$L), sets
!                S SEL($9), then "-SELECT CURRENT UNIT": loads
!                S UNIT N($12) and plants it in S UNIT($10) with
!                connective 0101.  Returns through K G LOCR's B,$,
!                which is the half word printed p.159 line 21's
!                "K LOCAT SIC,K G LOCR" loads.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THIRTY-FOUR LINES, TWENTY-EIGHT CARDS, AND NOTHING FELL OFF
! EITHER END -- THREE INDEPENDENT WAYS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! The SURVEY SAID 27 ROWS, 220057.40..220105.40.  It is short by
! seven rows and it lost line 1 at BOTH ends of its range: the
! page's first row is 220057.00, not 220057.40.  Counted off the
! card-serial column at 500 dpi the page runs IE000047 (line 1) to
! IE000074 (line 34), consecutive, with SIX serials printed twice
! -- one card, two statements:
!
!   IE000051  lines  5,6    SIC,K G LOCR     ; B,K G LOC
!   IE000056  lines 11,12   LVI,9,Z STEVL    ; SVA,9,K LOCTD
!   IE000057  lines 13,14   SIC,S RET AD($12); B,K LOCAT
!   IE000058  lines 15,16   KVI,4,.32        ; BZXE,$+1.32
!   IE000060  lines 18,19   SIC,E IND R      ; B,E IO IND
!   IE000061  lines 20,21   SIC,K POSLD      ; B,K POST L
!
! Every one of the six is a SIC/branch or a test/branch pair, so
! the doubling is the programmer keeping a pair on one card.
!
! THE TOP is closed by the header: line 1's serial IE000047 IS the
! header's own "CARD ID IE000047", so no row is above line 1.  It
! is closed a second time by the heading row's LOCATION field,
! which reads 220057 and is line 1's word (it is NOT blank here,
! because line 1 is a located instruction and not a banner -- see
! docs/transcription_workflow.md 1).  And a third time by printed
! p.159, whose last line (line 50, 220056.40) is a half-word
! "B,K POST L"; a half word at 220056.40 leaves the counter at
! 220057.00, which is this page's line 1.
!
! THE BOTTOM is closed by arithmetic that does not depend on
! reading the blank paper: 22 single-group rows + 12 double-group
! rows = 46 half words = 23 words = 0o27, and 220057 + 27 =
! 220106.  The deck's assembled counter arrives at 220106.00, and
! printed p.161 line 4 prints "220106.00 * SLC" -- a printed
! SLC,$ at exactly that word.  See THE JOIN FORWARD at the end.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! GLYPHS -- WHAT WAS SETTLED, AND ON WHAT
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! This page opens round glyphs everywhere: "22C057.CC" for
! 220057.00, "COCCCO.40" for 000000.40, "215776.C3" for
! 215776.03, "001000.CC FO" for 001000.00 F0.  Every round glyph
! in a LOCATION field or in one of the two OCTAL fields of a
! BINARY OUTPUT group is a 0 with certainty (the octal-field
! argument, docs/transcription_workflow.md 2b rung 5).  Three
! glyphs needed more than that:
!
! (1) LINE 3's SECOND HEX BYTE IS "D0", PRINTED "DC", AND IT IS
!     SETTLED BY RUNG 4 -- THE SAME STATEMENT PRINTED TWICE ON ONE
!     PAGE.  Line 3 is "ST(BU,18),SCUARC($13)" and line 25 is
!     "ST(BU,18), S CU ARC($13)".  Same card, same instruction,
!     same first half word (000006.00 8D) character for character;
!     line 25's trailing byte is a closed "D0" and line 3's is an
!     open "DC", in the SAME character position off the SAME drum.
!     Ink alone varies, so line 3 is D0.  The assembler agrees
!     without being told: the deck below compiles both rows to
!     000006.00 8D 022000.20 D0.
!
! (2) THE OP BYTE IS IN THE SECOND GROUP, NOT THE FIRST, AND THAT
!     IS WHAT MAKES (1) SAFE.  Lines 2 and 24 are the clean
!     control: "L(BU,18),SARCAD($10)" and "ST(BU,18), S ARC AD
!     ($10)" print IDENTICAL first groups (000000.40 8A) and
!     differ only in the second group's byte -- 50 for L, D0 for
!     ST.  The first group's low nibble is the INDEX: 8A for
!     ($10), 8B for ($11), 8C for ($12), 8D for ($13), 89 for
!     ($9), confirmed on nine rows of this page.
!
! (3) LINE 11's ".63" AND LINE 12's ".23" ARE READ AS PRINTED, NOT
!     "corrected" to the ".03" that docs/transcription_workflow.md
!     quotes for an LVI.  That ".03" is an index-1 figure, and the
!     field is the J (INDEX) FIELD plus bit 18.  Measured on this
!     repository's assembler, varying only J:
!
!         LVI, 0,(8)215776.0  ->  215776.01 01
!         LVI, 1,(8)215776.0  ->  215776.03 01
!         LVI, 2,(8)215776.0  ->  215776.05 01
!         LVI, 4,(8)215776.0  ->  215776.11 01
!         LVI, 8,(8)215776.0  ->  215776.21 01
!         LVI, 9,(8)215776.0  ->  215776.23 01
!         LVI,15,(8)215776.0  ->  215776.37 01
!
!     so J prints as 2J (+1 for the immediate forms) in the octal
!     offset position, and the operand's bit 18 adds 0o40 on top.
!     Line 11 is 0o40 (Z STEVL's .40) + 0o23 (J=9) = 0o63; line 12
!     is 0o00 (K LOCTD's .00) + 0o23 = 0o23; line 9 is 0 + 0o03
!     (J=1).  The page's own lines 28 and 30 print 0o22 for LV,9
!     and V+,9 -- the same J, one bit lower because they are not
!     immediate -- against two different operands, which is the
!     page checking the reading against itself.
!
!     THE CONSEQUENCE FOR THE EXTERNALS: because the field is J and
!     bit 18, an index instruction observes an operand's WORD and
!     its HALF WORD and nothing below.  Measured:
!
!         S UN A = 0.0   ->  LV,9,S UN A($10)  prints 000000.22 3A
!         S UN A = 0.8   ->  LV,9,S UN A($10)  prints 000000.22 3A
!         S UN A = 0.32  ->  LV,9,S UN A($10)  prints 000000.62 3A
!
!     0.0 and 0.8 are indistinguishable; 0.32 is not.  Same for
!     K NORM on line 9 and Z STEVL on line 11.
!
! NOTHING ELSE ON THIS PAGE NEEDED SETTLING, because the deck
! reproduces all forty-six printed half words character for
! character on the first assembly -- see THE PRINTED LISTING.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE SECOND ASTERISK: LINES 7 AND 26, AND TWO MORE THINGS IT IS
! NOT
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Every line number carries an asterisk ("1*", "34*"); that is the
! ordinary column and is not the marker.  TWO lines carry a SECOND
! asterisk, in its own column to the right of the LOCATION:
! LINE 7 (220063.40) and LINE 26 (220077.00).  Established by
! pixel count in that column alone at 300 dpi -- 218 and 208 dark
! pixels on those two rows against 0 on the other thirty-two --
! not by eye.
!
! docs/listing_typography.md 12 records the marker as open with
! eight things it is not.  This page adds two, both refuted from
! INSIDE the page so no neighbour has to be consulted:
!
!   * NOT "the row before a labelled entry point".  Line 7 does
!     precede K ILEGL and line 26 does precede K POSLD -- but line
!     10 precedes K K LOC and line 22 precedes K POST L, and
!     neither is marked.
!   * NOT "the row that ends on a word boundary".  Line 7 (a half
!     word at .40) and line 26 (a full word at .00) both do, and
!     so do lines 5, 9, 11, 13, 19, 21, 24, 25 and 33, unmarked.
!
! It is also two more nails in the pitch reading, which
! listing_typography.md already calls dead: the pitch here is 19
! on a 34-LINE page, where printed p.150 had 19 and 5 on a 28-line
! page and printed p.3 had 22-23 on 52 lines.  And the two marked
! statements have nothing in common -- line 7 is a half-word
! unconditional branch, line 26 a full-word VFL connective.
!
! RECORDED AND NOT THEORIZED.  No rule is proposed from this page.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WITNESSES -- C22-6728 IS TYPESET AND COVERS THIS ROUTINE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! The MCP System Analysis Guide charts the locate routine as
! FIGURE 94 and describes it in prose on its printed p.172.  It is
! a different press and a different ink, so it is a genuinely
! independent witness for SPELLINGS, unlike the volume OCR of this
! same listing.  Counting whole-token hits across both revisions
! (docs/ocr/C22-6728*_MCP_Sys_Analysis_Guide.txt, blanks squeezed
! out of names there as the guide prints them):
!
!   KILEGL 31   KKLOC 30   KLOCAT 28   KGATE 30   KNORM 24
!   ZSTEVL 32   SRETAD 39   SSEL 18    SUNA 15    SUNIT 11
!   SIOINS 10   SCUARC 8   SARCAD 7    KPOSTL 3   SUNITN 2
!   SLOCSU 2    KLOCTD 2   KGLOC 1
!
! Eighteen of this page's twenty-three distinct names, confirmed
! off a typeset page.  The prose is decisive about the semantics
! as well, and the match is card for card:
!
!   "If the status evaluation routine is being used, the
!    appropriate entry in the branch table should be B, KKLOC,
!    where the routine at KKLOC sets the KLOCAT return to ZSTEVL,
!    and sets SRETAD in the event the equipment is disk."
!                                       -- C22-6728 printed p.172
!
!   Figure 94, one box:  "SET KLOCAT RETURN TO ZSTVL, SET SRETAD
!                         TO KKLOC+2.0"
!
! Lines 11-14 ARE those sentences, and the "+2.0" is checkable:
! K K LOC is 220065.40, the SIC on line 13 saves the IC of the
! half word after line 14's branch, which is 220067.40, and
! 220065.40 + 2.0 = 220067.40.  The guide's own index entry reads
! "KKLOC+2.0".  That is a typeset document agreeing with this
! page's LOCATION column to the half word.
!
! FOUR NAMES THE GUIDE DOES NOT CARRY, and what holds them up:
!
! ALL FOUR WERE RENDERED FIRST HAND off printed p.159 at 600 dpi
! for this deck -- not taken from the volume OCR:
!
!   K ILEGL  printed p.159 line 6, rendered here: "220022.00
!            220064.32 C0  BZXE,K ILEGL".  Bit 18 is 0, so that row
!            pins this page's line 8 to the half word 220064.00
!            from another page -- which matters, because lines 4
!            and 7 here branch to K ILEGL.32 and never to K ILEGL,
!            so without p.159 this page would show only the SECOND
!            half word of its own label.
!   K FINI   Figure 94 prints a box "KEINI" (C22-6728 OCR).  F and
!            E differ by one bar and that is an ordinary OCR slip,
!            so this is a weak-but-real typeset witness in the
!            right chart.  The strong one is printed p.159 line
!            18: "220032.00  220057.32 C2  BXE,K FINI", a card on
!            a DIFFERENT page naming this page's line 1 at this
!            page's address.  (A BXE pins bit 18 only, and it is
!            0; the WORD is what that row establishes.)
!   K G LOCR printed p.159 line 21 is "220033.40  220105.40 80
!            K LOCAT  SIC,K G LOCR" -- byte for byte this page's
!            line 5, from another page.  It is a SIC, so it names
!            220105.40 to the BIT: this page's line 34.
!   K POSLD  printed p.159 line 49, "220056.00  220100.00 80
!            SIC,K POSLD" -- again a SIC, so 220100.00 is pinned
!            to the bit; this page's line 27 is at 220100.00.
!   K POST L printed p.159 line 50, "220056.40  220074.10 00
!            B,K POST L" -- a branch, so bit 18 only (it is 0);
!            this page's line 23 is at 220074.00.  That row is
!            p.159's LAST, and the half word it occupies is what
!            leaves the counter at this page's 220057.00.
!
! >>> CORRECTED 2026-10-31: THIS PAGE FIRST READ IT "E IC IND". <<<
! printed p.156 landed in the same batch spelling the same address
! "E IO IND", and check_symbol_spellings caught the pair -- a
! conflict NEITHER page could see, because each transcriber saw only
! its own sheet.  THE TYPESET MANUALS SETTLE IT, 11 to 1: C22-6728,
! C22-6728-1, C22-6678-1 and the MCP user's guide spell KIOIND
! eleven times and KICIND once.  Different press, so rung 2 of the
! glyph ladder is a genuine second reading here.
!
! The ink agrees once it is read properly.  printed p.189's defining
! card prints "E IC IND" -- but THAT ROW IS DROPPING INK: its own
! data description prints "BU,1CC,1C" where the values must be
! BU,100,10, and its value field prints "+00C00000".  C-shaped
! glyphs in fields that cannot hold a C.  Dropout OPENS a closed
! glyph and never closes an open one, so that C is a damaged O.
! printed p.156 line 4's comment reads "-CHECK I? INDS" and another
! page glosses the routine "CHECK IF SUCCESSFUL END OP" -- an
! end-of-operation test, which is I-O, not instruction-counter.
!
! AND THE TWO EXTERNALS NOBODY HAD PINNED, E IND R AND E IO IND,
! ARE DEFINED BY CARDS ON printed p.189 (PDF p.196), found by
! grepping the ADDRESS and not the name:
!
!   "221370.00+ ... BU,100,10   E IO IND  SYN,K IO IND"
!   "221371.00+ ... BU,40,10    E IND R   SYN,K K IND"
!
! and that page's own comment card prints the calling sequence
! this page uses on lines 18-19:
!
!   "- CALLING SEQUENCE  **  SIC,E IND R ; B,E IO IND"
!
! So both are aliases: E IO IND for K IO IND at 221370.00 (whose
! defining instruction, "K IO IND L(BU,2),S IO IND($13)", prints
! at 221370.00), and E IND R for K K IND at 221371.00 (whose
! "K K IND BRZ,$" prints at 221371.00).  Both SYN cards print
! their 24-bit VALUE, so these are addresses read off a card, not
! back-derived from a branch.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE REPO ALREADY BELIEVED ABOUT THIS PAGE, AND A LOOP THIS
! RENDER CLOSES
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! A CLAIM ABOUT THE REPO, cheap for the caller to check: FOUR of
! this page's seven labels were ALREADY carried as externals by
! landed decks, at exactly the addresses printed here --
!
!   decks/mcp_bootstrap_p127.strap  KILEGL  (8)220064.0
!   decks/mcp_bootstrap_p151.strap  KILEGL  (8)220064.0
!                                   KKLOC   (8)220065.40
!   decks/mcp_bootstrap_p152.strap  KILEGL  (8)220064.0
!                                   KKLOC   (8)220065.40
!                                   KGLOC   (8)220100.40
!                                   KGLOCR  (8)220105.40
!
! THAT IS NOT A COLLISION WAITING TO HAPPEN -- it is four more
! cross-page checks the merge will run for free.  strap/
! mcp_image.py's merge() treats a SYN for a symbol some other page
! PLACES as a STAND-IN and fails only if the two values disagree
! ("FAIL <sym>: <page> SYNs bit N, <page> places it at bit M").
! All four agree to the bit, so when p.160 enters MCP_IPL_PAGES the
! merge gains four checked stand-ins and loses four externals.
! (A bare `assemble(p152 + p160)` DOES fail, on "symbol 'SLOCSU'
! multiply defined" -- but that is the two decks both SYNing the
! same external and has nothing to do with these four labels;
! merge() is what deduplicates, not raw concatenation.)
!
! and all four agree with this page's LOCATION column exactly.  BUT
! READ THEIR NOTES BEFORE COUNTING THAT AS SEVEN WITNESSES: p.127's
! says "label row, printed p.160 (PDF 167)", p.152's cites "OCR
! line 8290" and "OCR line 8313" -- i.e. the VOLUME OCR OF THIS
! PAGE.  By docs/transcription_workflow.md rule 5 that is the same
! ink read by a worse reader, so those derivations were never
! independent of what is rendered here.  THE SAME HOLDS FOR
! ZSTEVL's ".40", which p.151 took from the OCR of THIS page's
! line 11.
!
! What IS independent, and what actually closes it, is the other
! half of each of those decks' notes: the BRANCH OR SIC ON THEIR
! OWN PAGE that reaches the address.  A branch pins bit 18, a SIC
! pins all 24 bits, and every one of them lands where this page
! prints the label.  So the loop is closed in the right direction
! now -- this render is the primary reading, and their rows are
! the check on it.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EXTERNALS -- every one pinned, and which bits are OBSERVED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE SIC MEASUREMENT, because it changes what two of these claims
! are worth.  docs/transcription_workflow.md, "WHAT THE ORACLE
! CANNOT SEE" 1, says an external back-derived from a branch or an
! LVI is known only to the HALF WORD.  SIC IS DIFFERENT.
! decks/mcp_bootstrap_p152.strap already says so in passing ("Line
! 25 is a SIC, which prints the BARE 24-bit address, so this row
! pins K G LOCR TO THE BIT") -- the credit is theirs; here it is
! MEASURED on this repository's assembler rather than asserted,
! everything else fixed and only the SYN's bit offset varied:
!
!     SIC,(8)221371.0   -> 221371.00 80     B,(8)221371.0  -> 221371.10 00
!     SIC,(8)221371.03  -> 221371.03 80     B,(8)221371.03 -> 221371.10 00
!     SIC,(8)221371.17  -> 221371.17 80     B,(8)221371.17 -> 221371.10 00
!     SIC,(8)221371.37  -> 221371.37 80     B,(8)221371.37 -> 221371.10 00
!     SIC,(8)221371.40  -> 221371.40 80     B,(8)221371.40 -> 221371.50 00
!
! A SIC prints its operand's FULL 24-bit address; a branch prints
! bit 18 and nothing below it.  So on this page E IND R's ".00" is
! OBSERVED to all six octal digits (line 18 is a SIC), while
! E IO IND's ".00" is observed only to the half word (line 19 is a
! branch) -- and is then supplied exactly by printed p.189's SYN
! card, which prints 221370.00+.
!
! S ARC AD   0.32       printed p.99 line 52's defining card,
!                       "S ARC AD SYN(BU,18),0.32 -ARC ADDRESS
!                       (DISK)"; a field offset, not an address.
!                       Lines 2 and 24 print 000000.40 (0o40 = 32)
!                       and the deck reproduces it.
SARCAD  SYN(BU,18), 0.32
! S CU ARC   6.00       printed p.102 line 19's defining card,
!                       "-CURRENT ARC"; landed in
!                       decks/mcp_bootstrap_p102.strap.  Lines 3
!                       and 25 print 000006.00.
SCUARC  SYN(BU,18), 6.00
! S SEL      0.39       printed p.99 line 32, "-SELECT FILE
!                       STATUS", a ONE-BIT field.  Lines 4, 26 and
!                       31 print 000000.47 (0o47 = 39) with three
!                       different index nibbles, so this page
!                       checks the offset three times over.
SSEL    SYN(BU,1), 0.39
! S RET AD   5.0        printed p.101 line 18, "-RETURN ADDRESS IN
!                       MCP", SYN(BU,19).  Line 13 prints
!                       000005.00 8C, and line 13 is a SIC, so all
!                       six octal digits are checked.
SRETAD  SYN(BU,19), 5.0
! S IO INS   4.0        printed p.101 line 17, "-IO INSTR. LAST",
!                       SYN(BU,64).  Line 23 writes S IO INS+.32
!                       and prints 000004.40 -- the +.32 is 0o40,
!                       so the base 4.0 is what the row checks.
SIOINS  SYN(BU,64), 4.0
! S UN A     0.0        printed p.99 line 20, "-UNIT AREA TABLE
!                       FIELD", SYN(BU,25).  Line 28 prints
!                       000000.22 3A; the .22 is the LV operation
!                       and index-9 bits, not the offset -- the
!                       page's own line 30, "V+,9,$L", prints
!                       000010.22 B0 with the SAME .22 against a
!                       different operand, which is what shows the
!                       .22 belongs to the "9" and not to S UN A.
!                       So this row observes the WORD only.
SUNA    SYN(BU,25), 0.0
! S UNIT     0.56       printed p.99 line 39, "-UNIT (MULTI UNIT",
!                       SYN(BU,3).  Lines 29 and 33 print
!                       000000.70 (0o70 = 56).
SUNIT   SYN(BU,3), 0.56
! S UNIT N   0.47       printed p.101 line 6, "-UNIT NUMBER",
!                       SYN(BU,3).  Line 32 prints 000000.57
!                       (0o57 = 47).
SUNITN  SYN(BU,3), 0.47
! S COMRG    215001.00  printed p.103's defining card; landed in
!                       decks/mcp_bootstrap_p103.strap.  Carried
!                       only because S LOC SU is defined off it.
SCOMRG  SYN, (8)215001.0
! S LOC SU   215001.17  "SUPPRESS LOCATE", bit 17 of the common
!                       region, as decks/mcp_bootstrap_p143.strap
!                       and others write it.  Line 17 prints
!                       215001.21 (0o21 = 17) -- and the operand
!                       of a VFL prints its FULL address, so this
!                       row checks the bit, not just the word.
SLOCSU  SYN(BU,1), SCOMRG.17
! K NORM     215776.00  a LANDED LABEL ROW: decks/mcp_bootstrap_
!                       p123.strap declares "!SYM KNORM 215776.00"
!                       off printed p.123's own LOCATION column.
!                       Line 9 here prints 215776.03 01; the .03 is
!                       LVI operation bits, so the bit offset below
!                       bit 18 is UNOBSERVABLE from this page and
!                       the ".0" is p.123's reading, not mine.
KNORM   SYN, (8)215776.0
! K GATE     215746.40  a LANDED LABEL ROW: decks/mcp_bootstrap_
!                       p123.strap declares "!SYM KGATE 215746.40".
!                       Line 10 here prints 215746.50 00: bit 18 IS
!                       set, so this page checks the HALF WORD
!                       against p.123 and does not assume it.
KGATE   SYN, (8)215746.40
! Z STEVL    221144.40  ITS OWN LABEL ROW IS PRINTED LATER IN THE
!                       VOLUME: "221144.40  000002.54 3C  Z STEVL
!                       LV,9,Z EVL MK($12) -GET MASK ADDR" (volume
!                       OCR of PDF p.195 -- an index, and the page
!                       is not transcribed yet).  Lines 11 and 22
!                       here print 221144.63 01 and 221144.50 00;
!                       both carry bit 18 set, so the half word is
!                       checked twice from this page.
!                       WORTH FLAGGING FOR THE CALLER: decks for
!                       printed pp.151 and 152 derived this ".40"
!                       from the volume OCR of THIS PAGE's line 11
!                       (OCR line 8290), which by
!                       docs/transcription_workflow.md rule 5 was
!                       not independent of this page's ink.  THIS
!                       RENDER CLOSES THAT LOOP: line 11 is read
!                       first hand at 900 dpi and compiles the
!                       printed word.
ZSTEVL  SYN, (8)221144.40
! K LOCAT    220033.40  printed p.159 line 21 IS the defining
!                       card, RENDERED FIRST HAND at 600 dpi for
!                       this deck: "220033.40  220105.40 80
!                       K LOCAT  SIC,K G LOCR".  Line 14 here
!                       prints 220033.50 00, bit 18 set, agreeing.
!                       That same p.159 row is also a SIC naming
!                       220105.40, which pins this page's line 34
!                       (K G LOCR) to the BIT from another page.
KLOCAT  SYN, (8)220033.40
! K LOCTD    220047.00  printed p.159 line 40 IS the defining
!                       label row, RENDERED FIRST HAND at 600 dpi:
!                       "220047.00  221144.50 00  K LOCTD
!                       B,Z STEVL".  Line 12 here prints
!                       220047.23 D0, whose bit 18 is 0, agreeing
!                       with it; and p.159 line 26's
!                       "BXE,K LOCTD-1.0" at 220046.32 is a third
!                       reading of the same word.
KLOCTD  SYN, (8)220047.0
! E IND R    221371.00  printed p.189's SYN card "E IND R SYN,K K
!                       IND", and K K IND's own instruction prints
!                       at 221371.00.  Line 18 is a SIC, so ALL
!                       SIX OCTAL DIGITS of the offset are checked
!                       here (see THE SIC MEASUREMENT above) --
!                       this is one of the few externals in these
!                       decks whose ".00" is a reading and not a
!                       convention.
EINDR   SYN, (8)221371.0
! E IO IND   221370.00  printed p.189's SYN card "E IO IND SYN,K
!                       IC IND"; K IO IND's own instruction prints
!                       at 221370.00 and the SYN prints its value
!                       as 221370.00+.  Line 19 is a BRANCH, so
!                       this page observes bit 18 only (it is 0);
!                       the rest comes from p.189.
EIOIND  SYN, (8)221370.0

        SLC, (8)220057.0             ! p.159 line 50 leaves here

KFINI   LCI,7,16                     ! line  1
        L(BU,18),SARCAD($10)         ! line  2  printed "SARCAD"
        ST(BU,18),SCUARC($13)        ! line  3  printed "SCUARC"
        BZBZ,SSEL($11),KILEGL.32     ! line  4
        SIC,KGLOCR                   ! line  5
        B,KGLOC                      ! line  6  same card as 5
        B,KILEGL.32                  ! line  7  (second asterisk)
KILEGL  LCI,7,(8)400                 ! line  8
        LVI,1,KNORM                  ! line  9
        B,KGATE                      ! line 10
KKLOC   LVI,9,ZSTEVL                 ! line 11
        SVA,9,KLOCTD                 ! line 12  same card as 11
        SIC,SRETAD($12)              ! line 13
        B,KLOCAT                     ! line 14  same card as 13
        KVI,4,.32                    ! line 15
        BZXE,$+1.32                  ! line 16  same card as 15
        CM0000,SLOCSU                ! line 17
        SIC,EINDR                    ! line 18
        B,EIOIND                     ! line 19  same card as 18
        SIC,KPOSLD                   ! line 20
        B,KPOSTL                     ! line 21  same card as 20
        B,ZSTEVL                     ! line 22
KPOSTL  L(BU,18),SIOINS+.32($12)     ! line 23
        ST(BU,18),SARCAD($10)        ! line 24  printed "S ARC AD"
        ST(BU,18),SCUARC($13)        ! line 25  printed "S CU ARC"
        CM0000(BU,1),SSEL($11)       ! line 26  (second asterisk)
KPOSLD  B,$                          ! line 27
KGLOC   LV,9,SUNA($10)               ! line 28
        L(BU,3),SUNIT($10),-18       ! line 29
        V+,9,$L                      ! line 30
        CM1111(BU,1),SSEL($9)        ! line 31
        L(BU,3),SUNITN($12)          ! line 32
        CM0101(BU,3),SUNIT($10)      ! line 33
KGLOCR  B,$                          ! line 34

! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE PRINTED LISTING, recorded so the oracle can check it later
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!   line  1  220057.00    000020.17 02                K FINI    LCI,7,16                        IE000047
!   line  2  220057.40    000000.40 8A  022000.20 50            L(BU,18),SARCAD($10)            IE000048
!   line  3  220060.40    000006.00 8D  022000.20 D0            ST(BU,18),SCUARC($13)           IE000049
!   line  4  220061.40    000000.47 8B  220064.74 04            BZBZ,S SEL($11),K ILEGL.32      IE000050
!   line  5  220062.40    220105.40 80                          SIC,K G LOCR                    IE000051
!   line  6  220063.00    220100.50 00                          B,K G LOC                       IE000051
!   line  7  220063.40 *  220064.50 00                          B,K ILEGL.32                    IE000052
!   line  8  220064.00    000400.17 02                K ILEGL   LCI,7,(8)400                    IE000053
!   line  9  220064.40    215776.03 01                          LVI,1,K NORM                    IE000054
!   line 10  220065.00    215746.50 00                          B,K GATE                        IE000055
!   line 11  220065.40    221144.63 01                K K LOC   LVI,9,Z STEVL                   IE000056
!   line 12  220066.00    220047.23 D0                          SVA,9,K LOCTD                   IE000056
!   line 13  220066.40    000005.00 8C                          SIC,S RET AD($12)               IE000057
!   line 14  220067.00    220033.50 00                          B,K LOCAT      -SELECT THE UNIT IE000057
!   line 15  220067.40    000000.51 04                          KVI,4,.32                       IE000058
!   line 16  220070.00    220071.72 C0                          BZXE,$+1.32                     IE000058
!   line 17  220070.40    215001.21 80  001000.00 F0            CM0000,SLOCSU                   IE000059
!   line 18  220071.40    221371.00 80                          SIC,E IND R                     IE000060
!   line 19  220072.00    221370.10 00                          B,E IO IND                      IE000060
!   line 20  220072.40    220100.00 80                          SIC,K POSLD                     IE000061
!   line 21  220073.00    220074.10 00                          B,K POST L                      IE000061
!   line 22  220073.40    221144.50 00                          B,Z STEVL                       IE000062
!   line 23  220074.00    000004.40 8C  022000.20 50  K POST L  L(BU,18),S IO INS+.32($12)      IE000063
!   line 24  220075.00    000000.40 8A  022000.20 D0            ST(BU,18), S ARC AD($10)        IE000064
!   line 25  220076.00    000006.00 8D  022000.20 D0            ST(BU,18), S CU ARC($13)        IE000065
!   line 26  220077.00 *  000000.47 8B  001000.00 F0            CM0000(BU,1),S SEL($11)         IE000066
!   line 27  220100.00    220100.10 00                K POSLD   B,$            -RETURN CONTROL  IE000067
!   line 28  220100.40    000000.22 3A                K G LOC   LV,9,S UN A($10)                IE000068
!                                                               -TURN ON SEL BIT FOR LAST UNIT
!   line 29  220101.00    000000.70 8A  003067.20 50            L(BU,3),S UNIT($10),-18         IE000069
!   line 30  220102.00    000010.22 B0                          V+,9,$L                         IE000070
!   line 31  220102.40    000000.47 89  001000.36 F0            CM1111(BU,1),S SEL($9)          IE000071
!   line 32  220103.40    000000.57 8C  003000.20 50            L(BU,3),S UNIT N($12)           IE000072
!                                                               -SELECT CURRENT UNIT
!   line 33  220104.40    000000.70 8A  003000.12 F0            CM0101(BU,3),S UNIT($10)        IE000073
!   line 34  220105.40    220105.50 00                K G LOCR  B,$            -RETURN          IE000074
!
! WHAT WAS HANDED TO strap_asm EXACTLY AS PRINTED, and taken:
! ALL THIRTY-FOUR STATEMENTS.  NOTHING WAS SUBSTITUTED, nothing
! was dropped, and no row was left failing.  The only editorial
! changes are the ones the deck format requires: blanks removed
! from names (the page itself prints the same symbol both ways --
! "SARCAD" on line 2 and "S ARC AD" on line 24, "SCUARC" on line 3
! and "S CU ARC" on line 25, "SLOCSU" on line 17 and "S SEL" on
! lines 4/26/31 -- which is IBM's own assembler telling us the
! blank is not part of the name).
!
! THE DECK REPRODUCES ALL FORTY-SIX PRINTED HALF WORDS CHARACTER
! FOR CHARACTER ON THE FIRST ASSEMBLY.  No assembler limitation
! was hit.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT COULD NOT BE RESOLVED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (a) THE SECOND ASTERISK on lines 7 and 26.  Measured, recorded,
!     and still unexplained; two more candidate rules die on this
!     page alone (above), and no rule is proposed.
!
! (b) THREE NAMES HAVE NO TYPESET WITNESS: K FINI, K G LOCR and
!     K POSLD.  (K POST L is thin but real -- KPOSTL appears three
!     times in C22-6728, twice as a Figure 94 box.  K FINI survives
!     only as Figure 94's garbled box "KEINI".)
!     Each is read a SECOND TIME off printed p.159's ink -- a
!     different card, a different page, the same drum -- which is a
!     second IMPRESSION but not a second PRESS.  If any of the four
!     is misspelled, nothing in this repository can currently say
!     so.  The cheapest thing that would: C22-6728's index pages
!     (around OCR line 45780 and 47840) list routine names with
!     page numbers, and a careful pass over them is unexplored.
!
! (c) BIT OFFSETS BELOW BIT 18 for K NORM, Z STEVL, K GATE, K LOCAT
!     and S UN A are UNOBSERVABLE from this page, by the index-
!     instruction measurement in GLYPHS (3) and by the branch rule
!     in docs/transcription_workflow.md.  They are supplied by
!     p.123's LOCATION column, p.159's LOCATION column, and a
!     later page's Z STEVL label row -- NOT by this page.  By
!     contrast E IND R, K POSLD, K G LOCR and S RET AD ARE pinned
!     to the bit here, because a SIC prints the bare address.
!
! (d) THE COMMENT ON LINE 28 is read as "-TURN ON SEL BIT FOR LAST
!     UNIT" at 500 dpi.  It is the longest comment on the page and
!     the only one this deck had to read near the right-hand rule;
!     "LAST" is the one word in it that a second reader should
!     re-check.
!
! (e) NOT A DEFECT, BUT WORTH SAYING OUT LOUD because the next
!     reader of these decks will meet it: S COMRG is carried at
!     TWO values across the repo -- (8)2151.0 in the decks for
!     printed pp.30-33 and (8)215001.0 in p.103's and onward.
!     This is the same block split that
!     decks/mcp_bootstrap_p150.strap records for D MCP (001472.00
!     inside the pp.2-98 tail, 000040.00 outside it), not a
!     disagreement about one word.  p.160 is in the MCP body, so
!     it takes 215001.0, and line 17's printed 215001.21 is this
!     page's own confirmation of that choice.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE JOIN FORWARD -- a falsifiable prediction for printed p.161
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 34 is a half-word branch at 220105.40, so THE COUNTER
! LEAVES THIS PAGE AT 220106.00.  Three ways to break that claim:
!
!   1. printed p.161's first LOCATED row should be 220106.00.
!   2. Its heading-row LOCATION field should be BLANK, because
!      p.161 opens with an asterisk banner (line 1 compiles
!      nothing) -- a blank there is NOT a refutation of (1); a
!      NUMBER there other than 220106 would be.
!   3. If p.161 prints its own "SLC,$", that row's LOCATION is the
!      counter arriving and must read 220106.00.
!
! The volume OCR of PDF p.168 carries "4  220106.00 *  SLC" --
! which is (3) and (2) together, and which also hands p.161's
! transcriber a second asterisk on that row.  That is an INDEX,
! not a witness; p.161's own render decides it.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------

!SYM   KFINI    220057.00
!SYM   KILEGL   220064.00
!SYM   KKLOC    220065.40
!SYM   KPOSTL   220074.00
!SYM   KPOSLD   220100.00
!SYM   KGLOC    220100.40
!SYM   KGLOCR   220105.40
!CHECK 220057.00 | 000020.17 02 | line 1 K FINI LCI,7,16 -- 16 decimal is word 0o20
!CHECK 220057.40 | 000000.40 8A 022000.20 50 | line 2 L(BU,18),SARCAD($10) -- first group's low nibble A is index $10; second group's byte 50 is the L operation (against line 24's D0 for ST)
!CHECK 220060.40 | 000006.00 8D 022000.20 D0 | line 3 ST(BU,18),SCUARC($13) -- printed "DC"; settled against line 25, the same card printed twice on this page
!CHECK 220061.40 | 000000.47 8B 220064.74 04 | line 4 BZBZ,S SEL($11),K ILEGL.32 -- the second group is a real internal check: K ILEGL.32 is line 8's label plus 32 bits, a forward reference into this page
!CHECK 220062.40 | 220105.40 80 | line 5 SIC,K G LOCR -- forward reference to line 34; a SIC prints the full 24-bit address, so this checks K G LOCR's bit offset as well as its word
!CHECK 220063.00 | 220100.50 00 | line 6 B,K G LOC -- forward reference to line 28; bit 18 set is K G LOC's .40
!CHECK 220063.40 | 220064.50 00 | line 7 B,K ILEGL.32 -- same target as line 4's second group, reached by a different operation (this LOCATION carries the second asterisk)
!CHECK 220064.00 | 000400.17 02 | line 8 K ILEGL LCI,7,(8)400 -- an (8) literal against line 1's bare decimal 16, same operation
!CHECK 220064.40 | 215776.03 01 | line 9 LVI,1,K NORM -- external; the .03 is LVI operation bits, so only K NORM's word and bit 18 are checked
!CHECK 220065.00 | 215746.50 00 | line 10 B,K GATE -- bit 18 set checks K GATE's half word 215746.40
!CHECK 220065.40 | 221144.63 01 | line 11 K K LOC LVI,9,Z STEVL -- index 9 prints .63 where line 9's index 1 prints .03; bit 18 set checks Z STEVL's .40
!CHECK 220066.00 | 220047.23 D0 | line 12 SVA,9,K LOCTD -- same index 9, .23 against line 11's .63; bit 18 clear checks K LOCTD's .00
!CHECK 220066.40 | 000005.00 8C | line 13 SIC,S RET AD($12) -- a SIC, so all six octal digits of S RET AD's offset are checked; low nibble C is index $12
!CHECK 220067.00 | 220033.50 00 | line 14 B,K LOCAT -- K LOCAT is printed p.159 line 21's own label at 220033.40; bit 18 set agrees
!CHECK 220067.40 | 000000.51 04 | line 15 KVI,4,.32 -- byte for byte the same card printed p.159 carries TWICE (its line 5, "220021.40  000000.51 04  K S LOC  KVI,4,.32", rendered here at 600 dpi, and again at its line 23, 220034.40)
!CHECK 220070.00 | 220071.72 C0 | line 16 BZXE,$+1.32 -- $ is 220070.00 so the target is 220071.40; bit 18 set, and this row checks the deck's own counter
!CHECK 220070.40 | 215001.21 80 001000.00 F0 | line 17 CM0000,SLOCSU -- a VFL operand prints its FULL address, so 0o21 = bit 17 of S COMRG is checked; the second group's 001000.00 is the all-zero connective against line 31's 001000.36
!CHECK 220071.40 | 221371.00 80 | line 18 SIC,E IND R -- a SIC, so E IND R's offset is OBSERVED to all six octal digits, not assumed (see THE SIC MEASUREMENT)
!CHECK 220072.00 | 221370.10 00 | line 19 B,E IO IND -- a branch, so bit 18 only; printed p.189's SYN card supplies the rest
!CHECK 220072.40 | 220100.00 80 | line 20 SIC,K POSLD -- forward reference to line 27, all 24 bits internal to this page
!CHECK 220073.00 | 220074.10 00 | line 21 B,K POST L -- forward reference to line 23; byte for byte printed p.159 line 50's word, which is that page's last row
!CHECK 220073.40 | 221144.50 00 | line 22 B,Z STEVL -- the same external as line 11 reached by a branch; the two rows agree on bit 18
!CHECK 220074.00 | 000004.40 8C 022000.20 50 | line 23 K POST L L(BU,18),S IO INS+.32($12) -- the +.32 lands as 0o40, which is what pins S IO INS at 4.0 rather than 4.32
!CHECK 220075.00 | 000000.40 8A 022000.20 D0 | line 24 ST(BU,18), S ARC AD($10) -- identical to line 2 except the operation byte, 50 vs D0: the L/ST discriminator, printed twice on one page
!CHECK 220076.00 | 000006.00 8D 022000.20 D0 | line 25 ST(BU,18), S CU ARC($13) -- byte for byte line 3's card, printed a second time; this is the row that settles line 3's "DC"
!CHECK 220077.00 | 000000.47 8B 001000.00 F0 | line 26 CM0000(BU,1),S SEL($11) -- same connective as line 17 on a different operand (this LOCATION carries the second asterisk)
!CHECK 220100.00 | 220100.10 00 | line 27 K POSLD B,$ -- a branch to itself, the half word the caller's SIC overwrites
!CHECK 220100.40 | 000000.22 3A | line 28 K G LOC LV,9,S UN A($10) -- the .22 is the operation and index-9 bits; see line 30
!CHECK 220101.00 | 000000.70 8A 003067.20 50 | line 29 L(BU,3),S UNIT($10),-18 -- the -18 offset prints as 0o67 in the second group, the only row on the page carrying an explicit offset
!CHECK 220102.00 | 000010.22 B0 | line 30 V+,9,$L -- $L is register word 0o10; the .22 is the SAME as line 28's, which shows the .22 tracks the "9" operand and not the address
!CHECK 220102.40 | 000000.47 89 001000.36 F0 | line 31 CM1111(BU,1),S SEL($9) -- 001000.36 against line 26's 001000.00 checks all four connective digits; low nibble 9 is index $9
!CHECK 220103.40 | 000000.57 8C 003000.20 50 | line 32 L(BU,3),S UNIT N($12) -- 0o57 = 47 pins S UNIT N apart from line 29's S UNIT at 0o70 = 56
!CHECK 220104.40 | 000000.70 8A 003000.12 F0 | line 33 CM0101(BU,3),S UNIT($10) -- 003000.12 is connective 0101 against line 31's .36 for 1111 and line 26's .00 for 0000: three of the sixteen checked on one page
!CHECK 220105.40 | 220105.50 00 | line 34 K G LOCR B,$ -- the half word printed p.159 line 21's SIC loads; the counter leaves at 220106.00
